/-!
# Signed simple matrices for the Parrott comparison

The eight tables are the candidates for `x_{±αᵢ}(1)` on the complete Geck
basis: four simple Cartan vectors, the 24 positive roots of `RootPartition.table`,
then their negatives. Each table is proved to be an involution. Their comparison
with the actual integral Geck curves is a separate statement,
`SimpleMatrixComparison`. It is an entrywise identity, with no assumption about
recognition or group structure. Transport of these eight identities along Weyl
routes can then identify all ten words of `Realization.assignment`.

Source: the simple-root formulas of `IntegralGeckConstruction`, GLS3 §§2.3–2.4,
and Parrott (1972), printed p.683. The tables were produced by the untrusted
`source/explore.py`; every asserted arithmetic identity is checked by Lean.
-/

